title: The Law for the Protection of the Republic
subtitle: The Reichstag votes on a law against the Republic's enemies.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 7
max-visits: 1
priority: 2

= The Law for the Protection of the Republic

Out of the anger of June comes a law. It bans organisations that plot against the Republic and sets up a State Court at Leipzig to try them. The SPD calls it the answer to the murderers. Our lawyers point out that it does not say which enemies it means. [? if bavaria_soviet != 2 : Bavaria has already said it will not apply it. ?]

The vote is on 18 July.

- @for: Vote for it.
- @against: Vote against it.

@for
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The SPD will remember our votes. So will the State Court.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids voting with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e22_protection_law = 1;
Q.spd_relation += 7;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The law passes with our votes. The first case before the new State Court is against the Organisation Consul. The second is against a communist printer in Halle.

@against
subtitle: We vote beside the nationalists, for the opposite reasons.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_protection_law = 2;
Q.spd_relation -= 5;
Q.independence += 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The law passes anyway. *Vorwärts* prints the division list on its front page, with our deputies' names next to Helfferich's.
